{"event": "turn", "session_id": "8dea4242ea8b4fd6a3d2f7b3f0dbb140", "sequence": 1, "created_at": "2026-10-16T06:16:32.974324+00:00", "message": "绿茶和红茶在制作工艺上有什么区别？", "resolved_question": "绿茶和红茶在制作工艺上有什么区别？", "context_turns": 0, "model": "deepseek-flash", "thinking": "disabled", "config_revision": 3, "compliance_blocked": false, "elapsed_seconds": 18.617, "model_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 4504, "output_tokens": 600, "response": {"answer": "绿茶与红茶在制作工艺上的核心区别在于**是否经过有意的酶促氧化（行业内常称为“发酵”）**。\n\n**绿茶**：鲜叶采摘后迅速加热（杀青），使酶失活，从而阻止氧化；之后可能经过揉捻、做形或粉碎、干燥等步骤。绿茶基本不进行有意的氧化。（来源：ISO 20715:2023 Tea — Classification of tea types）\n\n**红茶**：制作中会经历“发酵”环节。这里的“发酵”是行业用语，指叶片细胞破损后暴露于空气所发生的**酶促氧化**，与微生物发酵不同。红茶正是通过这一氧化过程形成其品质特征。（来源：Fermentation: The Key Step in Processing of Black Tea）\n\n**一句话对比**：绿茶以“杀青”终止氧化，红茶以“酶促氧化”为核心工艺步骤。\n\n补充说明：具体加热方式、做形方式会因产地和产品而异；另外，茶树品种与茶类是两个概念，同一品种用不同工艺可制成不同茶类，因此工艺对成品茶类型起关键作用。（来源：ISO 20715:2023；Impact of Six Typical Processing Methods on the Chemical Composition of Tea Leaves）\n\n如需了解具体某款绿茶或红茶的工艺或商品信息，可以告诉我茶名，我再帮你查询。", "intent": "question_answering", "intents": ["question_answering"], "confidence": null, "intent_source": "rules", "recommendations": [], "knowledge_sources": [{"title": "ISO 20715:2023 Tea — Classification of tea types", "url": "https://www.iso.org/obp/ui?_escaped_fragment_=iso%3Astd%3Aiso%3A20715%3Aed-1%3Av1%3Aen", "year": null}, {"title": "Fermentation: The Key Step in Processing of Black Tea", "url": "https://agris.fao.org/search/fr/records/6473b0a3542a3f9f03b31231", "year": null}, {"title": "Impact of Six Typical Processing Methods on the Chemical Composition of Tea Leaves", "url": "https://agris.fao.org/search/en/records/65dff5d763b8185d9cb04493", "year": null}, {"title": "Tea Board India — Modalities and Scheme Guidelines", "url": "https://www.teaboard.gov.in/pdf/schemes/Modalities_and_scheme_guidelines_12th_Plan.pdf", "year": null}], "memory_used": false, "clarification_required": false, "tasks": [{"id": "s1", "tool": "introduce_tea", "status": "succ